.TH start-cli-backup-target-create 1  "create "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-backup\-target\-create \- Create a backup target
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli backup target create\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a backup target
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Shared volume name
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
start\-cli\-backup\-target\-create\-local(1)
Create the volume on the data drive
.TP
start\-cli\-backup\-target\-create\-disk(1)
Create the volume on an external drive partition
.TP
start\-cli\-backup\-target\-create\-cifs(1)
Create the volume on a CIFS network share
